    'Check cashing store installations require specialized lenses that shoot clearly through bullet-resistant glass, audio intercom integration, and tamper-resistant hardware. Our Fort Worth technicians deliver high-security retail financial surveillance.',
    'We install and service video systems for check cashing stores, payday and title loan centers, wire transfer and remittance shops, and money services counters across Fort Worth, Arlington, Haltom City, Grand Prairie, Forest Hill, Everman, White Settlement, Saginaw, Watauga, Hurst, Euless, Bedford, Burleson, and Mansfield, including high traffic corridors along East Lancaster Avenue, Berry Street, Riverside Drive, Seminary Drive, Jacksboro Highway, and the retail strips off Loop 820, I-35W, I-30, and Highway 287. Teller windows get paired transaction and face optics engineered around bullet resistant glazing and lobby glare, with queue, drive lane, night drop, rear door, and safe room coverage included. Retention is configured with accurate transaction timestamps for dispute resolution and recordkeeping inquiries. Exterior hardware is rated for North Texas hail and triple digit heat, and our local crews export robbery footage for Fort Worth Police Department detectives the same day.',
